 "findings": [
  "Like for like (one thread, rendering inline): the Mac 1.91 ms per tick (vs) and 1.97 ms (Demo); Chromium 2.24 and 2.20 ms (1.12–1.17× the native build); WebKit 3.27 and 3.03 ms (1.5–1.7×); Node WASI 3.67 and 3.49 ms (1.8–1.9×). The native build is faster; every host is far inside the 60 fps budget (16.67 ms per tick; the game ticks every 33 ms). The Mac's default figures (1.33/1.55 ms on its game thread with rendering on a second thread; 3.2–3.3 ms CPU over all threads) are not comparable with the single-thread hosts",
  "The windows cover the same cycles on every browser and WASI run (vs 1064→1964, Demo 365→965) and the loaded counts match the Mac's (16,105 allocations, 12,817 bitmap requests, 2,072 audio requests, 621 files): the same work",
  "Startup: 'started' to 'loaded' takes 5.3–5.7 s in the browser and 4.1–4.7 s under Node WASI against 0.63–0.65 s on the Mac; the load itself (loadSeconds) is 0.57–0.81 s against 0.32 s. The difference lies before the load — where WASI computes the loading packages inline (every packaged file read and digested, ~726 MB, PortableSHA256 in wasm against CommonCrypto on the Mac; the Mac overlaps them with the menu) — not yet attributed between reads and digests (W3c)",
  "Memory: the module's linear memory reaches 1,617 MiB (vs) and 1,588 MiB (Demo) in both engines; whether a phone browser allows that (iOS Safari) needs a device"
 ],
